            "reply_data": [
                {
                    "author": {
                        "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?u=d09fd974c6720eba3039db6beb2f1c1efecdb51d&v=4",
                        "login": "echasnovski",
                        "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                        "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
                    },
                    "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
                    "body": "I'll mark this as an answer, since `laststatus=3` (i.e. \"global statusline\") indeed looks like the best suggestion here.\r\n\r\nI'd adjust the code, though:\r\n- The whole `eventignore` in `set_status` is probably too much and might be harmful in long term. I would go with something like this:\r\n\r\n    ```lua\r\n    local target_laststatus = vim.wo.diff and 3 or 2\r\n    if vim.o.laststatus ~= target_laststatus then vim.o.laststatus = target_laststatus end\r\n    ```\r\n\r\n- Not sure about if these events are enough. The `BufWinEnter` event might be also needed. And I haven't worked with built-in diff split, so don't know if `OptionSet pattern=diff` is enough here (it might be).",
                    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">I'll mark this as an answer, since <code class=\"notranslate\">laststatus=3</code> (i.e. \"global statusline\") indeed looks like the best suggestion here.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I'd adjust the code, though:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The whole <code class=\"notranslate\">eventignore</code> in <code class=\"notranslate\">set_status</code> is probably too much and might be harmful in long term. I would go with something like this:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"local target_laststatus = vim.wo.diff and 3 or 2\nif vim.o.laststatus ~= target_laststatus then vim.o.laststatus = target_laststatus end\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">target_laststatus</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">wo</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">diff</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">and</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">3</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">or</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">2</span>\n<span class=\"pl-k\">if</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">o</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">laststatus</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">~=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">target_laststatus</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">then</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">o</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">laststatus</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">target_laststatus</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">end</span></pre></div>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Not sure about if these events are enough. The <code class=\"notranslate\">BufWinEnter</code> event might be also needed. And I haven't worked with built-in diff split, so don't know if <code class=\"notranslate\">OptionSet pattern=diff</code> is enough here (it might be).</p>\n</li>\n</ul>",
                    "bodyText": "I'll mark this as an answer, since laststatus=3 (i.e. \"global statusline\") indeed looks like the best suggestion here.\nI'd adjust the code, though:\n\n\nThe whole eventignore in set_status is probably too much and might be harmful in long term. I would go with something like this:\nlocal target_laststatus = vim.wo.diff and 3 or 2\nif vim.o.laststatus ~= target_laststatus then vim.o.laststatus = target_laststatus end\n\n\nNot sure about if these events are enough. The BufWinEnter event might be also needed. And I haven't worked with built-in diff split, so don't know if OptionSet pattern=diff is enough here (it might be).",
